          "headline": "Senators vow to strip the 2027 budget as the House adds ₱5 billion to itself",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The budget fight moved to the Senate, where the majority bloc vowed on November 2 to remove 'corruption-prone' items and Malacañang warned Marcos may veto insertions without documents. Rappler then found the House added ₱5 billion to its own 2027 budget, and that 28 of 36 members who did not back Sara Duterte's impeachment face district public-works funds of no more than ₱300 million. Where roads get built now tracks how members voted.</p>",
