          "headline": "The impeachment court admits the prosecution's SALN and AMLC records",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The Senate impeachment court, in a November 5 ruling released on November 6, admitted most of the prosecution's documents, including Sara Duterte's SALNs and Anti-Money Laundering Council reports, while excluding two companies' corporate records. Prosecutors put the alleged unexplained wealth at about ₱818 million for 2022 to 2025. With one article left, the defense opens on November 9 against evidence the court has already let in.</p>",
