          "headline": "The Supreme Court upholds five-year barangay terms and moves the next polls to 2028",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The Supreme Court made public on November 6 a ruling upholding Republic Act 12326, which sets five-year terms for barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan officials and moves the next barangay and SK elections from November 2026 to November 2028. It was penned by Rodil Zalameda, whom Marcos had named chief justice a day earlier. Incumbent barangay leaders now hold over for two more years.</p>",
