          "headline": "Fil-Am candidates win in US midterms, mostly reelections",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>Filipino American candidates won a string of races in the November 3 US midterms, most of them reelections. Rob Bonta won another term as California attorney general, Virginia's Bobby Scott took an 18th term in Congress, and state legislators Erica Mosca in Nevada, Maria Cervania in North Carolina and Justin Jones in Tennessee were reelected. Several California local races were still being counted. The Fil-Am bench in US politics keeps widening.</p>",
